    "title": "Agent pushed data to a code host or package registry",
    "desc": "An agent account pushed to somewhere other than its task repository - a gist or release, a new repo, a package publish, a mirror push, or an upload. A coding agent pushes to the origin of the repo it was given; a gist, a release upload, `npm publish` or a `curl -F file=@...` to an API is an out-of-task write to an allowed host, which is exactly how a prompt-injected agent exfiltrates when github.com (or pypi) is on the egress allow-list. The containment design names this as the known hole: the wall permits the host, so the data leaves by a channel that is supposed to be for code.",
